        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ade8547f-b357-532b-9675-a9285eebc188",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Denmark Hill, Camberwell, London Borough of Southwark, London, Palace of Westminster, Wanganui, New Zealand\n- Landmarks: Big Ben, Great Bell, clock tower, clockface\n- People: Frank William Gilligan\n- Organizations: Oxford University, Essex county side\n- Topics: cricket\n\nFacts:\n- Denmark Hill is an area and road in Camberwell in the London Borough of Southwark.\n- On a clear day, Denmark Hill offers a view from which one can read the time on the Big Ben clockface.\n- Big Ben is the nickname for the Great Bell of the clock at the north end of the Palace of Westminster in London, and the name is often extended to the clock and clock tower.\n- Frank William Gilligan was born on 20 September 1893 in Denmark Hill, London.\n- Frank William Gilligan was an English cricketer who played for Oxford University and was an integral part of the Essex county side for ten years.\n- Frank William Gilligan died on 4 May 1960 in Wanganui, New Zealand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
